  "visual_review": "Inspected both material sheets and the placed-block three-way close-up from the published Oculus 1.8.8/Beddium 1.0.11 companion-bridge runs. Native Hardened Glowstone block emission is visibly stronger than ordinary Glowstone and the identical alpha-zero gold block. All five tool silhouettes show bright gold heads or blades and retain dark handles; individually worn armor shows luminous gold panels with dark openings and recognizable piece shapes. Held armor icons retain faint gold emission at this camera distance, with all four fixed foreground measurements exceeding their alpha-zero controls. The block retains its original largely uniform gold diffuse appearance and separate face/edge shading. Ordinary Glowstone and lantern controls remain consistent across the pair. All fifteen source comparisons pass; full thirteen-alpha ZIP audit, matched shader settings, frozen clock, exact current production classes, shader toggles and separate companion-on distance evidence authenticated. The alpha-zero retry completed and cleaned up without forced termination."
}
